# Diagrammo Slate — dark
# Generated from dgmo/src/palettes/slate.ts; the same sixteen slots that
# diagrammo.app/slate/ publishes. Do not hand-edit a hex here — change the
# palette in dgmo and take the file from the site.
#
# Normal (0-7) comes from the palette's LIGHT spectrum and bright (8-15) from
# its DARK one: a palette's light values are its darker ones and its dark
# values its lifted ones, which is exactly the normal/bright relationship a
# dark terminal wants. Nothing here was invented, every normal clears 3.2:1 on
# this background and every bright 5.6:1.
#
# Two slots are not what their name suggests, both deliberately: purple stands
# in for magenta (a diagram palette has no magenta), and teal takes cyan
# because the palette's steel cyan sits too close to blue, which it would keep
# landing beside. Steel cyan stays a diagram color.
#
# This replaced a version whose normal and bright bands both came from the dark
# spectrum, leaving red, green, magenta and cyan rendering identically in both
# — so anything using a bright variant for emphasis lost the distinction.

